  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ee810d15-63fb-5e27-b02d-d0ed782c6aa2" activityNameId="e8cf9231-70bd-5c41-b571-1b19c626f24c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Uranium enrichment diffusion plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Uranium enrichment diffusion plant
The data on material and energy requirement for construction are taken from an old US reference using a "model diffusion plants" and are amplified by a factor of 1.2 to take into account the differences in the installed capacity of the currently operating diffusion plants (EURODIF and USEC Paducah). The land use corresponds to the USEC plant, which is presumably the most consistent with the material inventory. It is assumed that 75% of reinforced concrete is dumped as non-contaminated waste from decommissioning.;
UUID: 2d38d217-9665-31dc-adbb-229750e0e3a6
The module includes: estimated land use of a plant with capacity of 8750 t SWU (separative work unit); energy (electricity, diesel, and light oil) and material requirements for the construction of the facility; transport requirements during construction; energy and transport requirements (for non-contaminated inerts concrete with reinforcing bars) during decommissioning; disposal of the non-contaminated inerts. The non contaminated metals are assumed to be recycled.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Available construction material and energy data, used as basis for this extrapolation, refer to a model plant in early 1980s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2d38d217-9665-31dc-adbb-229750e0e3a6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
